# The ENV program of the documentation flow (flow.md §4.1, §4.15): the
# module tree docs-src/flow/docs.flow.cx's acts resolve through.
#
#   cx flow validate docs-src/flow/docs.flow.cx --env docs-src/flow/docs.env.cx --allow-read=.
#
# An ORDINARY CX program — `cx --allow-read docs-src/flow/docs.env.cx` prints the
# inventory below, so the tree a run resolves against is readable without
# running it. The [?lib … :as docs] import is what names the acts
# `docs/<def>`; a relative [?lib] path resolves against the WORKING
# DIRECTORY, so every caller runs from the repository root (RULED: CICD-1).
[?lib './docs-src/flow/docs-acts.cx' :as docs]

[acts of='docs-src/flow/docs.flow.cx'
  [act name='docs/generate' pivot=true
       does="make docs-generate under --mode=write; nothing under --mode=check"]
  [act name='docs/check'
       does='make TARGET for every target the step names, each red one reported']
  [act name='docs/assemble'
       does='make site-check: render the guide, assemble site/, list it against its manifest']]
